WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.635
-How is everything, by the way,
with the quarantine?

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.103
Are you okay?

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:06.672
-You know, I got this --
as soon as it happened,

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:09.842
I bought this tiny little cabin
up in Montana,

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:14.981
and you know, it keeps me
way far away from anybody.

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:17.883
I don't see a human soul,
really, up here.

00:00:17.883 --> 00:00:18.985
It's fantastic.

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.887
I bought it from
a guy named Kaczynski.

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:23.256
It was kind of a mess
when I got it, but...

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:26.025
No Wi-Fi or cable.

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:27.960
It's like the guy
hated technology.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.562
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.964
Did you get it fairly cheap,
or is it...?

00:00:31.964 --> 00:00:33.532
-Yes, I did.
Yes, I did.

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:35.501
But I'm getting fat.
That's the problem.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.336
Are you getting fat
during this COVID thing?

00:00:37.336 --> 00:00:38.505
I'm getting a little fat.

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.406
My head never gains weight,

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:43.843
which is fantastic
for this Zoom medium.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:46.178
-Yeah.
-But, yeah, down here,

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:48.581
I'm starting to, like --
I'm ordering some of those

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:52.018
rocking chairs they sell outside
of Cracker Barrel restaurants.

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.620
You know, the extra wide ones.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.087
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:55.087 --> 00:00:56.589
-They're almost comedy ones.
You go, "who would sit in that"

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:59.859
-For that big, wide
all-American ass.

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:01.994
You know?
It's great.

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:06.399
And I just go, "More biscuits!
More biscuits!"

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:07.633
I love that place.
-More biscuits.

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:09.535
I love Cracker Barrel
restaurant, man.

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:12.205
It's the greatest.
-"More Biscuits" is the sequel

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.173
to "Memoirs and Misinformation."
-"More Biscuits."

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:16.509
That's right.
-"More Biscuits" is the sequel.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:19.646
Hey, by the way, we were talking
about some of the celebs

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:22.582
that you bring up in the book.
-Yeah.

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:26.618
-Did you get any --
Anyone getting mad at you

00:01:26.618 --> 00:01:28.454
for bringing --
You know, like --

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:30.256
-No, I think they're reacting
pretty well.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:33.860
Like, pretty much like this,
I think.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.328
"Huh?!"
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:36.328 --> 00:01:39.732
-"What the hell is this?!
Wha-- What?!

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.601
Oh!
Oh!

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:44.203
What did he --
[ Gasps ]

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:47.840
Oh!
Oh!

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.343
Why, I oughta!"
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:51.978
There's a lot of that going on.
-Uh-huh.

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:55.114
-Except for Gary Busey,
who's going like this --

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:58.384
"If you wear it on your head
when you're hang-gliding,

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:01.687
it'll blow your mind open
like a lobster dinner."

00:02:01.687 --> 00:02:05.358
-The audiobook here
is done by Jeff Daniels,

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:06.526
who, obviously...
-Yes.

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:07.694
-...you worked with,
"Dumb and Dumber."

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:10.596
And I love Jeff Daniels.
He's an amazing actor.

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:14.033
His quote -- [ Laughs ]
He was quoted as saying,

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:17.803
"I had no idea Jim
knew so many big words."

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:20.840
-Yeah, I heard about that.
To that I say,

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.577
Pneumonoultramicroscopic-
silicovolcanokoniosis.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.245
Do you know what that word is?

00:02:26.245 --> 00:02:28.581
-Pwkk!
No.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:32.218
-Well, maybe you should call
Jeff and find out if he knows.

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.353
-I just know that I'm not gonna
play Scrabble with you.

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:37.790
-It's the biggest word
humanity has ever produced,

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.091
and I know it.

00:02:39.091 --> 00:02:40.293
-[ Laughs ]
Oh, my God!

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:41.427
-That's all I'm saying.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:42.829
-You don't have to be
so cocky about it.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.331
-I feel like I had
to defend myself there.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:48.000
-I wasn't attacking.
-That's right.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.404
A lot of people don't know
that I've reached my apotheosis.

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:53.672
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:53.672 --> 00:02:58.744
Jim, what do you hope readers
take away from the book?

00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:01.481
-Gosh, uh, I hope they...

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:05.150
they, uh, have a great, great...

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:06.819
great time, honestly.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:08.521
I want them to have a good time.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:13.525
I want them to be so struck
by this strangeness

00:03:13.525 --> 00:03:18.163
and the invention of this book
that they rip their nipples off

00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:20.199
and run into the streets,
screaming my name.

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:21.667
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:23.736
-And then, when they get hit
by the car, and they lay there,

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:25.071
they can't even remember
their own name,

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.839
and that's really all I'm after.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.307
-You're not asking much.

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:33.079
-I want us all to be nameless,
one thing, joined in alchemy.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:34.413
-Wow.

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:38.551
-I will say,
the last page, which I won't --

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:41.187
[ Laughing ]

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:42.755
The last page --
-God, he's really gotten

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.657
out of control with this.
-No, no.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:47.226
I think you're not even close
to where you belong yet.

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:48.695
-It's fantastic.
And you know what?

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:51.264
It is like a lobster dinner.
It really is.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:54.567
'Cause once you think you're
full and you've eaten it all,

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:57.036
you'll realize
there's meat in the legs!

00:03:57.036 --> 00:04:00.639
-[ Laughing ]
-There's meat in the legs.

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:04.376
And the fantasy continues.
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:04.376 --> 00:04:07.180
-How'd you come up
with the cover, by the way?

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:10.249
-Oh, the cover.
The cover is a wild story.

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:12.885
That cover is actually my face

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:15.354
after being told
that I have 10 minutes to live.

00:04:15.354 --> 00:04:16.788
And that's for real.

00:04:16.788 --> 00:04:19.992
That was a missile test --
Sorry. Not a missile test.

00:04:19.992 --> 00:04:22.594
A fake missile alert in Hawaii.
-Yes.

00:04:22.594 --> 00:04:23.896
-I was there.
-No!

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.766
-I was writing.
My assistant, Linda, called me.

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:29.735
She was crying. She said,
"We have 10 minutes left."

00:04:29.735 --> 00:04:31.370
And I said, "What do you mean."

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:32.905
She said, "The missiles
are coming from North Korea."

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.039
-I remember this.
They sent out

00:04:34.039 --> 00:04:35.274
an emergency text to everybody.

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.075
-It was completely real to us.

00:04:37.075 --> 00:04:41.580
And I went -- You know,
my brain started winding.

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.716
And I tried
to get off the island.

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:47.019
And my daughter --
I couldn't get off the island.

00:04:47.019 --> 00:04:49.055
And then,
the question was posed,

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:50.189
"Should we all try
to get together."

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.091
I said, "I don't want to die
in my car."

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.392
And we had to say goodbye.

00:04:53.392 --> 00:04:58.463
And I sat on the lanai
and looked out at the ocean,

00:04:58.463 --> 00:05:01.601
and at that point,
I started going,

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:04.036
"Okay. Well, what can I do
with this last moment of time?"

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:06.706
And I just decided to go through
a list of gratitudes,

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:12.478
and honest to God,
I just could not stop thinking

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:14.514
of wonderful things
that have happened to me

00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:18.117
and blessings that I've had,
so it was lovely.

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:20.753
It was lovely.
And I got to a point of grace

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:23.322
with about two minutes to spare
when I found out

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:25.425
it wasn't actually happening.

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:28.494
And all I was planning to do was
close my eyes an be thankful,

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:30.829
'cause it's been a good ride.

00:05:30.829 --> 00:05:32.265
-What did you do
when you found out

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:34.233
that it was a fake missile test?

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:36.235
-Then I got pissed off,
and heads rolled.

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:38.570
[ Both laugh ]

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.639
-"I had a kegger, dude!"

00:05:40.639 --> 00:05:42.708
-[ Laughing ]
Exactly!

00:05:42.708 --> 00:05:44.577
Yeah.
"I smoked a tree!"

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:46.979
-[ Laughing ]

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:50.850
It is so creative.
It's so fun.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.919
You re-read pages over.

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:55.721
I laughed --
-And there's meat in the legs!

00:05:55.721 --> 00:05:57.824
-And there is meat in the legs.

00:05:57.824 --> 00:06:00.826
Ladies and gentlemen, that is
the one and only Jim Carrey.

00:06:00.826 --> 00:06:02.461
Thank you so much
for coming on our show.

00:06:02.461 --> 00:06:04.496
I really appreciate it, buddy.
-So great to see you, man.

00:06:04.496 --> 00:06:06.098
-So great to see you.
-And way to go on all of this

00:06:06.098 --> 00:06:08.567
and keeping it alive
and keeping the energy flowing

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.036
and making people happy.
Congratulations.

00:06:10.036 --> 00:06:11.537
-Thank you, buddy.
Thank you so much.

